From 1a963eb8917d46b73d2bf42a040ee8cd33634b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: john <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:39:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] client: BADGE=1 build for the WHY2025 badge (step A)

A slim client for the badge's NOMMU Linux (RV32, uClibc-ng, static bFLT,
no C++), gated behind one Make variable so a plain build is unchanged:
-DLOWMEM (no 18 MB crapto1 tables), 128K-sample graph buffers, smaller
demod and rx buffers, -Os without unwind tables, pthread spinlock shim,
GUI stubs as C, 128 KB stacks for the uart threads, and no Lua, hardnested,
static-nonce attack, MQTT, USART or PIV. Client-side Mifare key recovery
(darkside, nested, hardnested, autopwn, supercard) needs 18-128 MB of heap
and is left out of the command table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
